  "findings": [
    "Current build enables NEWPET and NEW_PET_EDITS. Mob EXP alone can level; item EXP is separate. Explicit evolution at stage ceiling increments one level and clears both EXP counters.",
    "Ordinary level-up under NEW_PET_EDITS does not roll bonus growth. This phase never changes any bonus/skill/age/lifetime state.",
    "Eleven seals are shared between growth-capable native code and the frozen quest. The quest calls pet.summon (fixed PetSystem), not newpet.summon (NewPetSystem); no newpet calls were found in the frozen Lua files. This is an unresolved source dispatch conflict, not permission to silently enable growth or reclassify live behavior. The previous quest-reference inventory is not a definitive behavior mapping.",
    "Item type37 is not a growth-seal discriminator: it contains twelve skill books and a transport box in the frozen source.",
    "Hatch code uses egg+300; five egg proto value0 fields disagree. Offline import must resolve explicitly. No runtime item-number arithmetic is introduced.",
    "Transport retains old pet row ID in socket1 and packs displayed properties into narrow attributes. These cannot replace the complete persisted pet row.",
    "minAge column is used as a UTC age-start timestamp, not a duration. Existing names and pet state rows are not emitted here, only counts and row hashes.",
    "Growth progression is disjoint instance state. A future writer must update only level, stage and EXP fields, preserving name, bonuses, skills, lifetime, age, recall and transport state.",
    "Growth lifecycle, hatching, food, skills, revive, enchant, transport and skins remain separate work; no existing content was converted or installed."
  ],
